title: EvilTokens device-code phishing kit
severity: critical
score: 80
tags: consent-phishing, phishing, eviltokens
attack: T1566.002, T1528, T1550.001
description: The page drives an EvilTokens-style device-code backend on a non-Microsoft host
  (/api/device/gate, /api/device/start, /api/device/status/<session>) and either sends
  the kit's X-Antibot-Token header (its fingerprint, sent even when the gate shows a
  decoy), gets a Microsoft device code back, or sends the visitor to Microsoft's device-
  code sign-in. The victim signs in to Microsoft for real while the kit polls /token for
  their tokens.
---
// A device-code kit backend (device_code_kit_hosts) plus one more sign of the kit.
device_code_kit_hosts
| where exists(device_code_relays)
    or antibot_header > 0
    or exists(device_code_handoffs)
    or exists(device_code_lure_frames)
